# AEIOS constitution (draft)

Full text: [docs/context/01-master-constitution.md](docs/context/01-master-constitution.md). Load 01 then 02–05 before architecture work. Conflicts: [docs/context/CONFLICT_MATRIX.md](docs/context/CONFLICT_MATRIX.md).

AEIOS is a closed-loop environmental intelligence system, not a passive logger or air-quality dashboard.

Do not collapse to: read sensors → upload → dashboard.

Preserve the loop: sense → quality → cross-modal confidence → adaptive decision → new measurement → explanation.

Patent-relevant interactions to keep testable: (A) cross-modal confidence + conditional activation + information-value-per-energy, (B) enclosure thermal/airflow affecting quality, (C) GPS-less spatial reconstruction from configured coordinates.

Supporting tech (LoRa, ESP32, Pi, SQLite, generic ML) is not the invention.

Before a feature: modular? testable without hardware? offline? observable? provenance kept? adaptive loop intact? no fake accuracy?

Prefer extensible architecture over shortest code. Do not add abstraction for its own sake.
